course: dictionary
lesson: 6830
title: Reading about places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The outback is a huge, dry, mostly empty part of Australia, far inland and far from the cities and the coast. «Most of the middle of Australia, called the Outback, is hot and dry.» The clues tell you where it is: the middle of the country, away from the sea.
explain: Read the words around it for more clues. «The outback is the huge dry middle of Australia: red sand, low bushes, rare rain and heat that can bake the ground.» These clues show a harsh place, yet it is full of animals that have found clever ways to live there.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you change outback to "the wet beach", the sentence stops making sense, so the outback must be dry and far from the coast.
fact: The outback is the dry, mostly empty middle of Australia, far from the coast.
fact: «The outback can burst into flowers after rare rains.» So the land can change a lot after rain.
fact: «Some frogs dig into the ground and wait years for the next rain.»
fact: Towns in the outback are very far apart, so people carry lots of water when they travel.
fact: Children in the outback sometimes do school by radio or internet, because their homes are so far from a school.
exercise: «Most of the middle of Australia, called the Outback, is hot and dry.» Where is the outback? | *The dry middle of Australia, far from the coast | The wet edge of the sea | A city in the south of Australia | A country in Europe
exercise: Which is most likely to be found in the outback? | *Red sand and low bushes | A big harbour with ferries | Tall skyscrapers | A busy train station with crowds
exercise: Why should you carry lots of water in the outback? | Water makes you run faster | The sun is cold there | *Towns are very far apart | Kangaroos need it from you
test: The outback is a huge, dry land that is far away from what? | *The cities and the coast | Rivers | Mountains | Farms
test: Where do most Australians live, according to the sentence about the Outback? | *Near the coasts, in cities such as Sydney and Melbourne | In the middle of the desert | In the outback | On a far island
exam: Which best describes the outback? | A small green park in a city | A town with many shops | *Huge, dry and mostly empty land far inland in Australia | A cold sea near Sydney
